{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-60919",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We're given a part and a whole, and we must find a percentage. So, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=\\text{part}÷\\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn this case, \n\n- the part is the number of unripe watermelons, which is $16,$ and\n\n- the whole is the total number of watermelons, which is $200.$\n\nSubstituting our numbers into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=16÷200=\\frac{16}{200}.\n$$\n\nTo write this as a percentage, we create an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{16}{200}=\\frac{16÷2}{200÷2}=\\frac{8}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{100}=8%\n$$\n\nTherefore, $8%$ of the watermelons were unripe.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
